# Ground-state SCF for fcc Cu in the CONVENTIONAL cubic cell (natom=4).
# First half of the two-run recipe that produces a phonon DDB like the
# bundled data/out_DDB.  Parameters reconstructed from that DDB's header
# (ecut 25 Ha, PAW with pawecutdg 50, 48 bands, Gaussian smearing
# tsmear 0.00367 Ha, ixc -1009); this file is a faithful template, not
# the literal historical deck.
#
# Provide your own Cu PAW pseudopotential with znucl 29 / zion 19 in
# pseudos/ (see README.txt).

#------------- Fundamental variables (header of the .in file) -------------
abcd     = cu_phonon_scf

#------------- Structure of the system ------------------------------------
acell    3*6.64968453          # conventional cubic a = 6.6497 Bohr = 3.5189 A
rprim    1 0 0                 # cubic (the DDB cell IS the conventional
         0 1 0                 # cubic cell; acell given in Bohr)
         0 0 1

natom    4
typat    1 1 1 1
xred
    0.00000000  0.00000000  0.00000000
    0.50000000  0.50000000  0.00000000
    0.50000000  0.00000000  0.50000000
    0.00000000  0.50000000  0.50000000

ntypat   1
znucl    29

#------------- Exchange-correlation and pseudopotentials ------------------
ixc      -1009                 # as recorded in the shipped DDB header
pseudos  "Cu_paw.psp8"         # <- your Cu PAW pseudo (zion 19)
usepaw   1
pawecutdg 50.0

#------------- Numerical parameters of the calculation --------------------
ecut     25.0
nband    48
occopt   3
tsmear   0.003674932248
iscf     7                     # SCF cycle as recorded in the DDB header
nstep    50
toldfe   1.0d-10

#------------- k-point grid ----------------------------------------------
# the shipped DDB was computed on a 256-point shifted grid; a standard
# 8x8x8 shifted grid is equivalent in spirit for this demo
kptopt   1
ngkpt    8 8 8
shiftk   0.5 0.5 0.5

#------------- Output -----------------------------------------------------
prtden   1                     # density for the DFPT run below
prtwf    0
optcell  0
dilatmx  1.0

%%
# Run:  abinit cu_phonon_scf.in > cu_phonon_scf.log
# Then run cu_phonon_rf.in, which reads this density (getden -1).
